# Search Before Implementing

Before writing ANY new function, class, adapter, or connector, search these libraries:
  1. `unified-market-interface` — market data, venue adapters, canonical schemas
  2. `execution-service` — order management, CeFi/DeFi/sports execution adapters (formerly unified-trade-execution-interface, unified-defi-execution-interface, unified-sports-execution-interface)
  3. `position-balance-monitor-service` — position feeds (formerly unified-position-interface)
  4. `instruments-service` — reference data, instrument definitions (formerly unified-reference-data-interface)
  5. `unified-trading-library` — storage, secrets, pubsub, ConfigStore (formerly unified-trading-services)
  6. `unified-config-interface` — config schema, BaseConfig
  7. `unified-trading-library` — event logging
  8. `unified-cloud-interface` — cloud primitives, storage client, Tier 0 abstractions
  9. `unified-domain-client` — instruments, domain clients
  10. `unified-api-contracts` — external API schemas, VCR mocks
  11. `unified-features-interface` — feature definitions, feature store client
  12. `unified-feature-orchestration-library` — feature pipeline orchestration
  13. `unified-sports-reference-interface` — sports reference data adapters

If it EXISTS in a library: USE the library. Do NOT reimplement.
If the library version is WRONG: FIX the library. Do NOT add a workaround in the service.
If it is MISSING from a library: ADD it to the library first, then use it.

